cue0140606
00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:35.000
I consider him simply an outstanding Rabbi.

cue0140607
00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:37.000
I mean, as the Rabbi's Rabbi.

cue0140608
00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:42.000
I mean, the paradigm of how a Rabbi should function

cue0140609
00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:48.000
in a modern synagogue.

cue0140610
00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:49.000
Did you meet him?

cue0140611
00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:50.000
Many times.

cue0140612
00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:52.000
And I not only met him,

cue0140613
00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:56.000
I was very fond of him,

cue0140614
00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:59.000
and he was the one who recommended me

cue0140615
00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:05.000
to receive the postdoctorate fellowship at the seminary.

cue0140616
00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:06.000
Yes.

cue0140617
00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:13.000
So I am particularly very fond of him.

cue0140618
00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.000
He was a great writer, of course.

cue0140619
00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:26.000
Sepharadim are notorious for not appreciating Hachamat.

cue0140620
00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:28.000
People don't know Hachamat Lub al-Abadi

cue0140621
00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:30.000
never had a position as a Rabbi.

cue0140622
00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.000
He was a businessman.

cue0140623
00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:39.000
And they appreciated him in true Jewish fashion

cue0140624
00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:40.000
only after he died.

cue0140625
00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:41.000
After he died?

cue0140626
00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:44.000
Because he died without telling them anything.

cue0140627
00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:47.000
And once we went to Hachamat Lub al-Abadi,

cue0140628
00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:51.000
we wanted to go raise some funds for some money,

cue0140629
00:23:51.000 --> 00:23:53.000
I don't remember,

cue0140630
00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:54.000
and he tells me,

cue0140631
00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:55.000
come with me,

cue0140632
